WEBVTT

1
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:19.000
Nathan B.: Self-serve first. The pricing page draft is ready, but checkout still needs billing support for monthly plans.

2
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:26.000
Nathan B.: The target is to launch before the Q4 campaign starts on 2 November.

3
00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:21.000
Emma C.: 41% of new signups never create their first booking. I'll break the funnel down by step so we stop guessing.

4
00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:30.000
Emma C.: My bet is the calendar-connect step, but that stays a bet until we have the numbers.

5
00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:47.000
Daniel K.: So nearly half stall before the first booking. That's onboarding, not acquisition.

6
00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:48.000
Anna H.: Monthly billing is the unknown, so give me until Wednesday for a real estimate on monthly billing.

7
00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:28.000
Nathan B.: Then the launch stays on track for the week of 26 October, and the billing estimate decides whether it slips.

8
00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:51.000
Anna H.: Deal. No new scope on the self-serve tier until the estimate is in.

9
00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:54.000
Nathan B.: Agreed.

10
00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:36.000
Emma C.: Do annual plans need to be in the self-serve tier at launch?

11
00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:41.000
Nathan B.: I can't say before the billing estimate is in.

12
00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:38.000
Anna H.: Reminders: we switched the SMS provider last week, and failures dropped from 3.1% to 0.8%.

13
00:29:05.000 --> 00:29:10.000
Anna H.: I'll keep watching SMS failures for two more weeks.
